# tally 2.2.1 R18 (L §4.3: a move binds its keys in the order written; a read that states its own day needs no law
# date; the engine's move_read_dated):
# clause 1: "A read's keys and arguments are judged on their own": region in cal[region], in a key's on
# before the at, is law-dated: LOAD-LAWDATE (m3/fixes/lawdate/g1_b_on). tally 2.2: the guard.
=== options exit=1
=== g1_b_on.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..

index wk = day 2026-01-05..2026-01-11
index regions = [pl, de]

input fee: money PLN
input cal[r in regions]: calendar
input region: key regions
input d0: date
input d1: date
input rd[r in regions]: date reading

move pay[d in wk]: transfers
  on d
  at d
  leg cash from konto to shop amount fee

move one[p in accounts on add_business(d0, 1, cal[region])]: transfers
  on d1
  at lifespan(p).from
  leg cash from p to shop amount fee

move pay2[d in wk where false]: transfers
  on d
  leg cash from konto to shop amount fee

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  fee = 10.00 PLN
  d0 = 2026-01-02
  d1 = 2026-01-20
  rd[pl] = 2026-01-01 at 2026-01-01
  rd[de] = 2026-01-07 at 2026-01-07
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "w"

version c
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  region = pl
  cal[pl] = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
  cal[de] = calendar(weekends [sun])

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE move one's key p reads law-dated region with no law date: its at reads p (g1_b_on.tally:29)
